# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test fixtures are tracked on purpose
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The blanket `*.csv` and `*.json` rules above silently excluded every test
# fixture, so CI checked out the repo WITHOUT them. The backend suite then died
# at collection and NOTHING ran:
#   ERROR tests/indicators/test_parity.py
#   FileNotFoundError: tests/indicators/fixtures/ohlcv.csv
# Re-include fixture directories only; generated outputs stay ignored.
!stock-screener-ui/tests/fixtures/*.json
!stock-screener-ui/tests/indicators/fixtures/*.csv
!stock-screener-ui/tests/indicators/fixtures/*.json
!stock-screener-ui/tests/api/test_event_radar/fixtures/*.json
!stock-screener-ui/tests/api/test_event_radar/fixtures/*.csv
!stock-screener-ui/data/symbol_aliases.json
!stock-screener-ui/tsconfig.json
!stock-screener-ui/.oxlintrc.types.json
!stock-screener-ui/tsconfig.typecheck.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Root-level caches and local residue
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The ignore rules for these lived only in stock-screener-ui/.gitignore, so a
# `git add .` at the repo root could commit a 1 GB node_modules or test output.
# `reports/` is deliberately ignored, not deleted: the artifacts stay on disk.
node_modules/
test-results/
reports/
venv/

# SQLite WAL/SHM sidecars: live, transient, and unsafe to commit. The .db is
# tracked for the QA fixture; these two are rewritten on every write.
db/alphashri.db-shm
db/alphashri.db-wal
stock-screener-ui/db/alphashri.db-shm
stock-screener-ui/db/alphashri.db-wal
